<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Pathway xmlns="http://pathvisio.org/GPML/2021" title="CO₂ fixation into oxaloacetate (anaplerotic)" organism="cellular organisms" source="PlantCyc" version="20260304101735">
  <Xref identifier="PWYQT-4429" dataSource="MetaCyc" />
  <Description>&lt;i&gt;Supporting evidence for this pathway in Oryza sativa Japonica Group&lt;/i&gt;: This pathway is on the list of Ubiquitous Plant Pathways (UPP) that was generated for the COMET project, which includes pathways that are thought to be present in all or most land plants. All UPP pathways are automatically imported into databases regardless of Pathologic predictions. &lt;A href=&quot;https://www.plantcyc.org/about/savi-pipeline&quot;&gt;[more info]&lt;/A&gt; &lt;i&gt;Summary from MetaCyc:&lt;/i&gt; This anaplerotic pathway replenishes the intermediates of the TCA cycle. |FRAME: EC-4.1.1.31| (PEPC), is an enzyme often associated with photosynthesis in C4 plants such as |FRAME: TAX-4577| (see |FRAME: PWY-241|). However, in C3 plants, such as |FRAME: TAX-3702|, this enzyme plays a role in several processes such as replenishing depleted |FRAME: PWY-5690 TCA cycle| compounds that have been used for nitrogen assimilation or other tasks |CITS: [17894783][20202167]|. The enzyme, which is the major anaplerotic source for the replenishement of TCA cycle intermediates, achieves this function by enabling the fixation of |FRAME:CARBON-DIOXIDE| into |FRAME:OXALACETIC_ACID|. Since the enzyme accepts only |FRAME: HCO3| molecules, |FRAME:CARBON-DIOXIDE| needs to be converted to |FRAME: HCO3| by the enzyme |FRAME: CPLX-7750| |CITS: [10515911]|. The pathway also plays an important part in some autotrophic bacteria and archaea such as the thermophilic methanogenic archaeon |FRAME: TAX-145262|. The organism is an autotrophic anaerobe that can grow on a gas mixture of |FRAME:CARBON-DIOXIDE| and |FRAME: HYDROGEN-MOLECULE| as its carbon and energy sources, respectively. It possesses two oxaloacetate-synthesizing enzymes, |FRAME: CPLX-7747| and |FRAME: CPLX-7743| |CITS: [9478969]|.</Description>
  <Authors>
    <Author name="zhang" />
    <Author name="SRI" />
    <Author name="tissier" />
    <Author name="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE" />
